# ThreadSanitizer suppressions (TCP4.13b).
#
# tokio's IO-driver readiness protocol (ScheduledIo::set_readiness and the
# driver turn loop) is a known TSan false-positive class: the intrusive
# atomic protocol is not modelable by TSan, and every frame in the reported
# races sits inside tokio/std internals (first seen: nightly run
# 30070025008, executor hub_clone_behavior binary). Suppression is
# function-scoped — a race whose stack touches any Strata frame still
# reports and fails the lane.
race:tokio::runtime::io::scheduled_io
